{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 58, :comments ["<b>And the plague is removed from them.</b> If when they washed it the first time at the priest's instruction, the plague departed from it entirely." "<b>And it shall be washed a second time.</b> A term of immersion. The Targum of 'washing' throughout this parashah is a term of laundering — ״וְיִתְחַוַּר״ — except this one, which is not for laundering but for immersing; therefore its Targum is ״וְיִצְטַבַּע״. And so all washings of garments that are for immersion are translated ״וְיִצְטַבַּע״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:20.535658487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}